# ForkChop environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored. Never put real values in this file — it is
# committed, and only variable NAMES belong here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Supabase
#
# BROWSER-SAFE. Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ and are sent to the client on purpose.
# The anon key is a public project identifier, not a secret: it grants nothing
# on its own because every table is protected by row-level security keyed on
# auth.uid().
#
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
#
# Leave both unset and the app still runs, signed out, saving to localStorage.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Newer Supabase projects issue a publishable key (sb_publishable_...); older
# ones issue an anon JWT. Either works — set whichever your project shows under
# Project Settings → API. The publishable name is preferred if both are set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# NOTE: the Supabase *service role* key bypasses row-level security entirely.
# It is not used anywhere in this app and must never be added as NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Database
#
# SERVER-ONLY. Optional. Where the bundled recipe corpus is seeded to.
# Serverless hosts are detected automatically and use the OS temp directory,
# so this normally does not need setting.
# FORKCHOP_DB_PATH=

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Spoonacular
#
# SERVER-ONLY. Note the deliberate absence of a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: that is
# what stops Next.js inlining it into the browser bundle. The browser reaches
# Spoonacular only through /api/recommendations, which acts as the proxy.
#
# Sign up at https://spoonacular.com/food-api/console#Dashboard
# Free tier is 50 points per day. Our query shape costs about 1.85 points for
# 10 full recipes, so roughly 27 searches a day before the quota is spent —
# which is why Spoonacular is only consulted when local results are thin, and
# why responses are cached for 10 minutes.
#
# Unset, the app searches only its own 60 bundled recipes — no error, no
# degraded UI, just a smaller catalogue.
SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Grocery
#
# SERVER-ONLY. Optional. Without these the Instacart and Walmart+ checkout
# options appear but report themselves as not connected.
# INSTACART_API_KEY=
# WALMART_API_KEY=
# FORKCHOP_GROCERY_PROVIDER=mock
